WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.789 align:start position:0%
 
i was fortunate enough to get my hands  on a review copy of the upcoming novel  tom clancy's the division recruited  i haven't done a book review before  other than required work in my days at  university but given my obsession with  the division story and the fact that  i've covered both of the previous books  in great detail i thought why not  written by thomas parrott i admittedly  was a little nervous when i first opened  this up as the previous two books had  been written by alex irvine and had  grown comfortable with his style of  writing and had no idea what to expect  from this new author's interpretation  however i was pleasantly surprised  [Music]  [Music]  the green poison epidemic that  originated in new york city has now  spread far and wide  washington dc was one of the next major  cities to be hit  much like new york it wasn't long before  dc's infrastructure began to collapse  police hospitals emergency services were  quickly overrun  the national guard was called in but was  unable to cope with the riots and  dwindling numbers through sickness  the government was falling apart and  what was left of it was evacuated from  the city the president has died and the  two who were appointed since have also  been reported as dead  however the sleeper cell agents of the  division are still active attempting to  save what remains  and despite their low numbers they have  been successful in pushing some of the  larger hostile groups back and out of  the city  although the identity and knowledge of  the shd's existence was among the  highest level of classified agencies it  has been months since the first wave was  activated and by this stage most people  have either witnessed or heard tales of  their activity across america  located in maryland mara kanghai is a  security expert who previously served in  the u.s navy  when things started getting bad she  rushed over to the enlistment officers  so she could do her part in helping  bring the situation back under control  but when she got there she realized it  was too late  the building was dark  all she found was a man in an officer's  uniform  slumped over the desk  he had clearly taken his own life rather  than succumb to the virus that was  ravaging the country  it was at this point that maya knew that  all she could do was to fall back and  ride out the situation at hand  to do her best to ensure that she and  her younger brother could survive  they would go on to move around from  building to building district to  district in search of a safe place that  they could call home  eventually they would join a community  of survivors  called athena  in time mara's past and the navy would  become known and much to her objections  she was placed in charge of athena's  security  protecting it from the scavengers and  hostile groups who only wanted to take  advantage of what was going on  unfortunately myra's time of head  security led to making some tough  decisions  some of these decisions required action  for the survival of the community  but would ultimately lead to the death  of members  including her own brother  one day while the team was returning  from a supply scavenging mission they  were followed by a large heavily armed  group wearing yellow hoods  myra's defensive preparations put up a  good fight but ultimately they were far  outgunned and quickly losing ground to  this invading group  fortunately for athena there just  happened to be a cell of division agents  who were active nearby  through a cloud of smoke and gunfire the  agents quickly dispatched the remaining  hostile forces  inside athena once the smoke had settled  myra talks with the agents  and finds out that they were actually  just passing through to carry out a  mission of grave importance  then before myra realizes what's  happening the next day she has agreed to  joining these agents in their mission  she doesn't exactly know what it is and  what she's signed up for but she's now  been given the chance to make a real  difference  the old way of recruiting agents is long  gone  the only way that new members can now be  recruited is out in the field  will myra be successful in overcoming  the tests and challenges thrown her way  or will she be overcome by the long line  of enemies who are plotting to put a  stop to the country's last line of  defense the division  thomas parrott has an amazing style of  writing  don't get me wrong i thoroughly enjoyed  the previous two novels written by alex  irvine  but this was something special  call me a classic stereotypical  millennial if you'd like but generally  i'm not so driven by fictional written  literature  i would usually prefer my fictional  entertainment to come in the form of  something interactive or with supporting  infographics images or even movies and  cutscenes  i prefer my general reading to go into  something that is more fact-based  learning education knowledge these are  the things that will generally drive my  reading experience  but parrot's work on this novel  absolutely hooked me in  sure there was a certain amount of  familiarity with the setting that drove  some of it  but the detail he went into when  describing scenes  i could picture in my head so clearly  that i struggled to put it down  i found myself hanging on to every word  actually it wasn't even so much the  detail i don't think that's the right  way of explaining it  the style and direction of how he  explained it it just met up with how my  imagination has been filling the gaps  with the division story up until now  i was so engaged that i found myself  reading through certain scenes faster to  match the action of what was playing out  in the story  and that i was actually feeling my heart  rate increase like i'd entered the dark  zone in the division 1 for the first  time  again i'm not familiar with the sort of  reaction through reading a book so bear  with me  a huge part of this has to be with how  the characters have been portrayed  all three of the main characters are  very easy to relate to  brenda the division's cell leader is  charismatic and strong but isn't without  her vulnerabilities and regrets about  the choices she has made in the past  leo is a strong silent type with a stoic  almost hostile way of expressing himself  to those around him  but deep down he is a heart of gold  trying his best to hide his utmost  respect and care for those in his team  while keeping the mission at the  forefront of his mind  and myra a strong but likable character  who like most others has gone through  absolute hell to survive this far  while she embraces a challenge ahead of  her at every turn she questions whether  she is capable either ethically morally  or physically  the story is told from myra's point of  view and although i thought i'd struggle  after following april callahar for so  long i found it a very easy transition  into her story  within only a few chapters i found  myself having formed quite a  relationship with each of them  the only thing about this novel that  didn't quite sit well with me was the  ending it just felt a little  anticlimactic  without going into detail it just sort  of ended  i don't know what i was expecting but i  wanted a little more  however this could be more of a  testament as to how much i was enjoying  the story rather than the ending being  no good  if you enjoyed the new york collapse and  broken door novels this book is for you  if i had to rank them i would say that  new york collapse was a bit different  due to all of the puzzles that needed to  be solved so it would be better to  compare it to broken dawn and out of the  two i found recruited to be far more  engaging  i'm actually looking forward to reading  through it again  don't get me wrong i like reading  fiction but i often find myself getting  bored with all the fluff they use to  fill the story and build the scene i  just never felt that way with this novel  am i just getting older and more chill  ready to embrace this sort of  entertainment  or is this a book that you really need  to check out  believe it or not i've kept the spoilers  to a minimum i've just attempted to set  the scene a bit more than the general  overview that were given on most  websites  the bulk of what i've talked about is  from early on in the book and there are  a number of details that are purposely  left out i'm not interested in spreading  any spoilers or leaks  i plan on covering the story in greater  depth after it's been released in  february 2022 but as always i'd  recommend reading the book as it will do  far greater justice to the story than i  will  i'll be tackling it from a narrative  point of view rather than through the  eyes of the agent and training  now for a hint of speculation i feel  like there may even be a little bit of a  teller as to why the fighting is  happening in the soon-to-be-released  division heartlands  the agents are headed in roughly the  right direction for this  so some of the events they came across  could be the reason  but i absolutely couldn't be sure  as there has been nothing officially  released on the upcoming title  that's something to talk about more in a  later video  thank you for watching i hope you've  enjoyed my first ever book review and  i'll catch in the next one  cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

